        "worked_solution": "To find every subset of $U,$ we list out every combination of elements within $U.$ \n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/assets/b0e483a2d10cba17fb2bd3bf0e78d7b4d2fc07b22dbb5c492564b998bbfce6fc.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,{-\\pi },{\\pi },{-\\pi ,\\pi }.\n$$",
