        "problem": "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that  ${x}_{3}=-3.$ Substituting this into the second equation,  we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(-3)=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2-2(-3)=-2+6=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(4)+3(-3)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-1-8+9=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=0$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=-3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$",
