        "knowledge_point": "Finding Unions and Intersections of Finite Families of Indexed Sets",
        "problem": "Find ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}$, given that $I={0,1,2},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{0}={0},\\,{S}_{1}=(0,1),\\,{S}_{2}=(0,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2} \\\\  & ={0}\\,\\cup \\,(0,1)\\,\\cup \\,(0,2) \\\\  & =[0,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
